{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/649642-editions-issue-got-second-edition-what-are-the-changes-between-second-third-20","id":649642,"title":"Editions Issue: got second edition. what are the changes between second/third/20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-02T20:04:51-07:00","id":649642,"title":"Editions Issue: got second edition. what are the changes between second/third/20?","content":"so yeah, a friend of mine sold me the second edition of werewolf the apocalypse which is pretty neat -dig the comics-. my Gm's used to use third edition though..<br /> so..any major changes i should bear in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T20:17:47-07:00","id":649675,"title":"","content":"Character creation has different rules, you start with less Gifts in 2nd Ed. There may be some other differences as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T20:19:59-07:00","id":649693,"title":"","content":"- Revised no longer requires a mirror to step sideways<br /> - Combat system - 2nd edition has all the quirks from before revised had close combat attacks adding successes to damage, which goes along with inflated weapon damage.<br /> - There are fewer Gifts overall in 2nd edition, as some, like Master of Fire, didn't get in until Revised.<br /> - One Gift is present that isn't in later editions, the Red Talon Gift Avalanche.<br /> - Some setting material was tweaked in later editions so that the Impergium wasn't quite so close to modern times and started much further back.<br /> - Rock song quotes. Rock song quotes, everywhere in 2nd edition. In Revised and after, not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T00:42:01-07:00","id":649808,"title":"","content":"There is the whole B/L/A thing and different way of marking them and healing them as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T08:35:31-07:00","id":650142,"title":"","content":"More things I forgot:<br /> - Revised and W20 have Ancestors; this was called Past Lives in prior editions.<br /> - Pure Breed used to have an effect on human appearance before W20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/649642-editions-issue-got-second-edition-what-are-the-changes-between-second-third-20?p=649675#post649675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character creation has different rules, you start with less Gifts in 2nd Ed. There may be some other differences as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you still get three Gifts to start out with. Chargen hasn't changed much at all since 1994.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:03:40-07:00","id":654382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/649642-editions-issue-got-second-edition-what-are-the-changes-between-second-third-20?p=650142#post650142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Pure Breed used to have an effect on human appearance before W20.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what context ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Revised introduced some new elements, that weren't around in 2nd edition (like a Red Talon off-shot in Africa and Uktena amongst a minority people in Japan).<br /> <br /> Umbra revised changed the rules about brightness in the umbra in regards to 2nd Edtion and revised core rules - stating that it is bright in the Penumbra when it is daytime in the physical world.<br /> <br /> W20's biggest change, in my opinion, is that in clear contradiction to revised (and 2nd and before) that &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; can no longer identify pre-change cubs. Shifting the whole character creation greatly towards &quot;lost cubs&quot;, who until their first change weren't raised as garou. Also, there is the return of the mirroring surface.<br /> <br /> Revised for the first time stated, that a mother's breed solely determines the child's breed (unless it is metis). Allowing for a male wolf to father a human child with a homid female garou and correspondingly allowing for a human male to father wolf cubs with a lupus born female garou. Before revised there wasn't any statement on the matter, I believe, and most people I know assumed, that the species of the non-shifter parent determined the breed of the child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:34:27-07:00","id":654592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/649642-editions-issue-got-second-edition-what-are-the-changes-between-second-third-20?p=654382#post654382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what context ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Revised introduced some new elements, that weren't around in 2nd edition (like a Red Talon off-shot in Africa and Uktena amongst a minority people in Japan).</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's really perplexing that WW kept trying to cram monsters around the Ainu, seeing as how the most generous demographic estimates would allot perhaps one Garou or Fera by the statistical figures we've been given (one per 200K people). First it was the Stargazers, then the Uktena*, and then the problem hopped over across time and editions to Forsaken 2nd edition claiming that being an Uratha in Japan is pretty much hand in hand with being Ainu.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Between them and the Wendigo, the Wendigo would be more likely to be found there, since the Ainu are related to people from around Kamchatka, and Rage Across Russia gave us Wendigo in this region.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T03:06:35-07:00","id":654947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/649642-editions-issue-got-second-edition-what-are-the-changes-between-second-third-20?p=654382#post654382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what context ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Revised introduced some new elements, that weren't around in 2nd edition (like a Red Talon off-shot in Africa and Uktena amongst a minority people in Japan).<br /> <br /> Umbra revised changed the rules about brightness in the umbra in regards to 2nd Edtion and revised core rules - stating that it is bright in the Penumbra when it is daytime in the physical world.<br /> <br /> W20's biggest change, in my opinion, is that in clear contradiction to revised (and 2nd and before) that &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; can no longer identify pre-change cubs. Shifting the whole character creation greatly towards &quot;lost cubs&quot;, who until their first change weren't raised as garou. Also, there is the return of the mirroring surface.<br /> <br /> Revised for the first time stated, that a mother's breed solely determines the child's breed (unless it is metis). Allowing for a male wolf to father a human child with a homid female garou and correspondingly allowing for a human male to father wolf cubs with a lupus born female garou. Before revised there wasn't any statement on the matter, I believe, and most people I know assumed, that the species of the non-shifter parent determined the breed of the child.</div> </div> </div> </div> Revised started indicating that if your character had the Pure Breed background and were Silver Fang, he pretty much had to be Russian. If he were Shadow Lord, he had to be Carpathian, etc.<br /> <br /> And the issue with Breed of the mother being the deciding factor was based off the need to keep the shapeshifter locked into form for several months. They added a Rite to allow for the 'non shapeshifter' to be the deciding factor in another book. (Though I don't remember which one.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}